hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"258","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa or Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her. On her authority, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness in which he died: “They poured on me seven sacrifices whose vessels were not permissible. “Perhaps I will rest and be with the people.” Aisha said: “So we made him sit in a copper basin made of copper, and we poured water over him from them until He started indicating to us that we had done so, then he left. Muhammad bin Yahya related it to us, and said: I heard Abd al-Razzaq mention it, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. Likewise, except that he did not say: “of copper” when he made the hadith undoubtedly narrated on the authority of Urwa."
